cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Tumor-from-EEG: a reproducible workbench for quantitative EEG biomarker
  extraction and subject-disjoint machine-learning evaluation
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kooklan
    given-names: Soheil
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5035-7833'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/soheilkooklan/Tumor-from-EEG'
abstract: >-
  Research software for quantitative EEG (qEEG) biomarker extraction and honest
  machine-learning evaluation. Computes 81 documented biomarkers across time,
  spectral, time-frequency, entropy and complexity domains, applies staged
  feature selection with stability analysis, and evaluates classifiers under
  repeated subject-disjoint nested cross-validation with probability
  calibration, bootstrap confidence intervals and paired significance testing.
  Not a medical device; the brain-tumour application is an untested hypothesis,
  as no public EEG dataset with imaging-confirmed tumour labels exists.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - quantitative EEG
  - biomarkers
  - machine learning
  - reproducibility
  - data leakage
  - cross-validation
  - explainable AI
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-01'
